+# @deepseek-ai/dsh-vision-bridge
+
+English | [中文](README.zh.md)
+
+An opt-in visual sub-agent bridge for text-only main models. DSH stores each uploaded image through the existing attachment service, persists one adjacent `<system-reminder>` for every new image-bearing human message, and exposes `vision_inspect` so the main model can delegate a complete visual question to an administrator-configured OpenAI-compatible vision model. The main model never receives image tokens: DSH's text-only projection replaces every image block with a stable text handle, while the durable reminder carries the full current-session `attachment_id`.
+
+The bridge is disabled in the base bundle. Leave it disabled for native multimodal routes; those routes continue using DSH's native image path without this reminder or tool.
+
+## Configuration
+
+Enable the existing base-bundle row in a later composition patch and restate its complete config:
+
+```yaml
+- id: vision-bridge
+  disabled: false
+  config:
+    baseURL: !!js process.env.DSH_VISION_BASE_URL
+    apiKeyEnv: QWEN_VISION_API_KEY
+    model: Qwen3.6-35B-A3B
+    timeoutMs: 120000
+    maxImagesPerCall: 9
+    maxOutputTokens: 4096
+```
+
+`baseURL` is required when the row is enabled; `/chat/completions` is appended unless it is already present. `apiKeyEnv` is a credential reference, resolved per call through `ctx.credentials` or the immutable launch environment. A literal `apiKey` is supported for controlled embedding but should not be committed. The numeric bounds fail loud unless they are positive integers.
+
+Loading the row is the enablement decision. It supplies the optional `imageInputBridge` admission capability, registers `vision_inspect`, and installs the durable reminder hook. There is no model preset or global prompt mutation.
+
+## Durable history and KV cache
+
+The reminder is generated only while a newly claimed human message contains image blocks. It is inserted immediately after that message and appended by the ordinary agent loop as another durable `user/message`. Later turns replay that exact event; the plugin does not remove, regenerate, move, or re-inject old reminders. Thus the prior conversation remains an append-only request prefix and can reuse the same KV-cache entries as ordinary text history.
+
+Compaction may replace an old visible range with a summary according to the deployment's normal policy. The attachment authorization check still examines the complete session event log, including shadowed events, but the summary must preserve any `attachment_id` the main model may need later.
+
+## Session isolation and gateway contract
+
+Before reading bytes, `vision_inspect` resolves every requested id from uploaded image blocks in the calling agent's own session event stream. An unknown or cross-session id rejects the complete batch before any attachment read or gateway request. Duplicate ids and over-limit batches also fail before dispatch.
+
+The gateway receives one OpenAI-compatible chat-completions request containing the main model's complete delegated prompt plus data URLs for the authorized images. Model-visible results contain only `attachmentIds`, `summary`, `observations` (`text`, optional `region`, optional `confidence`), and `limitations`; endpoint, credential, remote model, timing, and internal error bodies are excluded.
+
+## Model Experience
+
+### Upload reminder
+
+#### What the model sees
+
+Each newly uploaded image message is followed by one durable notice containing full current-session `attachment_id` values. No notice is added after a tool result.
+
+##### Reminder template
+
+```markdown
+<system-reminder>
+本条用户消息包含图片，已保存到当前对话：
+- attachment_id: <full attachment id>，name: <optional escaped name>
+主模型不能直接读取图片像素。需要视觉信息时调用 vision_inspect；不需要时继续处理用户请求。
+</system-reminder>
+```
+
+#### Token effect
+
+One bounded text notice is added for each image-bearing human message; each image contributes one id line. Old notices remain ordinary durable history and are not generated again.
+
+#### KV Cache effect
+
+Append-only: the new user message and notice extend the reusable request prefix. Subsequent turns replay the exact stored events without mutation or reordering.
+
+### vision_inspect tool
+
+#### What the model sees
+
+The model sees the `vision_inspect` tool with `attachmentIds` and a complete delegated `prompt`; its description says to reuse recent tool results unless a new visual question, region, comparison, or missing observation requires another call.
+
+#### Token effect
+
+The stable tool definition is present whenever the plugin is loaded. Each successful call adds one structured textual tool result; image bytes and data URLs exist only in the separate vision-gateway request.
+
+#### KV Cache effect
+
+The stable tool definition is part of the reusable request prefix. Each new tool call and result is appended normally, without rewriting earlier reminders or observations.
+
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+- **Compaction depends on identifier-preserving summaries** — the attachment remains authorized from the full event log, but the main model cannot choose a shadowed image if its compact summary drops the full `attachment_id`.
+- **One configured visual backend** — routing among multiple vision models, health-based failover, and per-workspace overrides are deferred.
+- **OpenAI-compatible transport only** — provider-native upload APIs and server-side image caches are not implemented.
+- **No automatic visual call** — the main model decides whether the user's task needs pixels; the bridge does not invoke the vision backend merely because an image was uploaded.
+- **Explicit enablement is deployment-wide** — do not enable the bridge row for a process intended to rely on native multimodal input.
